  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Prismatic light lab",
    "overview": "Studio X OS brings photography's physical light, optical depth and considered composition into a commercial software introduction. Charcoal working surfaces, blue/lavender light and opal display type carry the supplied Studio X OS marks. The personality is futuristic and confident, with the real product remaining legible beneath the spectacle.\n\nThis is the commercial homepage's scoped visual authority. It does not replace, merge into or redefine the personal Team Alpha system in [`frontend/DESIGN.md`](../../frontend/DESIGN.md) or its product context. The homepage's Persuade strategy, centered composition, intentional hero-to-dashboard gap and detailed scene choreography remain in the [surface brief](../STUDIO_X_OS_HOMEPAGE_MOTION.md). This document records reusable visual decisions; it does not turn one page's arrangement into a rule for every Studio X OS screen.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Physical optical materials around the exact supplied X artwork.",
      "Distinct display and working-interface typography.",
      "Open editorial chapters interrupted by truthful sample product surfaces.",
      "Responsive and keyboard-stable alternatives to cinematic motion.",
      "Clear preview, sample-data and coming-soon qualifications."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Material Roles Rule",
        "body": "Resolve text, controls, boundaries and focus through the semantic recipe for the surface they sit on. Do not copy the dark studio focus or muted ink into the opal client material without checking contrast.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Display Pairing Rule",
        "body": "Use Manrope for commercial display hierarchy and Inter for working controls. Do not introduce the personal site's Playfair Display as a commercial heading face.",
